{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788348498915,"sessionID":"ses_f9e20155cffePEnQZzaxI6Q8lc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2f32d77d3faa41e789e84a67","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/SKILL.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/SKILL.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: name: pyasc-syntax-constraints\n3: description: pyasc Python syntax support and restrictions reference. Documents supported and unsupported Python syntax within @asc2.jit functions, type constraints, and ConstExpr usage. Trigger — when writing kernel code, checking if a Python construct is supported, or debugging JIT compilation errors related to syntax.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # pyasc Syntax Constraints\n7: \n8: Syntax and keyword support varies across v2 snapshots. For CANNBench, the\n9: source of truth is `integrations/cannbench/pyasc-v2-source` at the commit in\n10: `SOURCE_COMMIT`; load `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` and verify uncertain constructs\n11: against that source plus the exact-v2 compile gate. In particular, its\n12: `asc2.range` supports `unroll_factor` and `gm_barrier`, but not `parallel`.\n13: \n14: ## Overview\n15: \n16: pyasc compiles Python code to Ascend C via JIT. Only a subset of Python syntax is supported inside `@asc2.jit`-decorated functions. This skill documents what is and is not allowed.\n17: \n18: ## Supported Syntax\n19: \n20: | Syntax | Example | Notes |\n21: |--------|---------|-------|\n22: | Attribute access | `nums.__len__()` | |\n23: | `while` loop | `while i < n: ...` | |\n24: | `for` loop | `for i in asc2.range(n): ...` | Use `asc2.range()` inside kernel, not `range()` |\n25: | Binary operators | `a + b * c` | `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`, `//`, `**`, `&`, `\\|`, `^`, `<<`, `>>` |\n26: | Unary operators | `~a`, `-a`, `not a` | |\n27: | `tuple` | `return x, y, z` | |\n28: | `list` | `nums = [a, b, c]` | |\n29: | `pass` | `pass` | |\n30: | Ternary `if` | `ans = x if x > 0 else 0` | |\n31: | `if`/`elif`/`else` | Full conditional blocks | |\n32: | Constants | `a = 1; b = True` | |\n33: | Comparisons | `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `==`, `!=` | |\n34: | Function calls | `func()` | Must be `@asc2.jit`-decorated or asc2 built-in |\n35: | Boolean logic | `and`, `or` | |\n36: | Augmented assign | `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, `%=` | |\n37: | Assignment | `x = expr` | |\n38: | Annotated assign | `count: int = 3` | |\n39: | f-strings + assert | `assert cond, f\"msg {val}\"` | |\n40: | Subscript | `nums[0]` | |\n41: | Slice | `tensor[offset:]` | |\n42: \n43: ## Unsupported Syntax\n44: \n45: | Syntax | Status | Workaround |\n46: |--------|--------|------------|\n47: | Nested functions | Not supported | Define separate `@asc2.jit` functions |\n48: | `global` | Not supported | Pass values as parameters |\n49: | `return` from kernel | Not supported | Kernels write to output tensors; device functions may return |\n50: | `return` inside `if`/`for` | Not supported | Use top-level return only in device functions |\n51: | `continue` | Not supported | Restructure loop logic |\n52: | `print()` | Not supported | Use `assert` with f-strings |\n53: | `with open(...)` | Not supported | Do file I/O outside JIT |\n54: | `raise` | Not supported | Use `assert` instead |\n55: | `try`/`except` | Not supported | Handle errors outside JIT |\n56: | `yield` / `yield from` | Not supported | No generators |\n57: | `lambda` | Not supported | Define named functions |\n58: | `break` | Not supported | Restructure loop logic |\n59: | `import` / `from...import` | Not supported | All imports outside JIT |\n60: | `async def` / `async with` | Not supported | No async |\n61: | `nonlocal` | Not supported | Pass values as parameters |\n62: | Class methods as kernels | Not supported | Use module-level functions |\n63: | If-scoped variables | Restricted | Initialize before `if`; use `asc.ConstExpr` for compile-time branching |\n64: | Unsigned int comparison | Restricted | Use `np.int64` or truthiness check instead |\n65: \n66: ## Type Constraints\n67: \n68: ### Kernel parameter types (runtime)\n69: \n70: | Supported | Not supported |\n71: |-----------|---------------|\n72: | `bool`, `int`, `float` | `str` |\n73: | `numpy` scalars and `ndarray` | `tuple`, `list`, `dict` |\n74: | `torch.Tensor` (NPU mode only) | Complex objects |\n75: | `asc.GlobalAddress` | |\n76: \n77: ### Compile-time parameters\n78: \n79: Use `asc.ConstExpr[T]` for values that must be resolved at compile time:\n80: ```python\n81: @asc2.jit(always_compile=True)\n82: def kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n83:     # tile_size is resolved at compile time and included in the JIT cache key\n84:     ...\n85: ```\n86: \n87: ### Built-in whitelist inside JIT\n88: \n89: Only these built-ins are available: `dict`, `float`, `int`, `isinstance`, `issubclass`, `len`, `list`, `range`, `repr`, `str`, `tuple`, `type`\n90: \n91: Note: For iteration inside `@asc2.jit`, use `asc2.range()` instead of `range()`.\n92: Do not assume optional keywords are portable between pyasc snapshots.\n93: \n94: ### Cube (matmul) loop + placement notes\n95: \n96: - **M/N/K tile loops are compile-time.** When the trip count is an\n97:   `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (matmul m/n/k tiles), a plain Python `for i in range(...)`\n98:   is fully unrolled at JIT time — that is the intended form for the loop that must\n99:   keep an operand resident in `L0A`/`L0B`. Use `asc2.range(...,\n100:   unroll_factor=2)` only on the *inner* tile loop you want software-pipelined\n101:   (double-buffered).\n102: - **Overlap (`gm_barrier=False`) doubles the pipelined L0 buffer.** The 2-deep\n103:   tile must fit half the L0 capacity (≤ 32 KiB for L0A/L0B, ≤ 64 KiB for the f32\n104:   L0C). A full-K `[256,128]` f16 L0B tile is 64 KiB and overflows when doubled\n105:   (`L0B overflow: 65536 bytes available, 131072 used`); shrink the tile (e.g.\n106:   `N_TILE=64`) before relying on overlap.\n107: - **Cube tile placement is explicit:** load/`asc2.copy` operands to\n108:   `asc2.TileLocation.L0A` (left) / `L0B` (right); stage from GM via\n109:   `asc2.TileLocation.L1` for reuse; the `@` result lands in L0C as f32 — cast with\n110:   `.to(asc2.float16)` before `asc2.store` if a 16-bit output is wanted.\n111: \n112: ## Kernel vs Device Function Rules\n113: \n114: | Rule | Kernel function | Device function |\n115: |------|----------------|-----------------|\n116: | Launched from | Host via `kernel[core_num](...)` | Other `@asc2.jit` functions |\n117: | `return` value | Not allowed | Allowed |\n118: | `@asc2.jit(...)` options | Effective (always_compile, etc.) | Ignored |\n119: | Nesting | Cannot be nested | Cannot be nested |\n120: \n121: ## References\n122: \n123: - [Supported Syntax Details](references/supported-syntax.md)\n124: - [Unsupported Syntax Details](references/unsupported-syntax.md)\n125: - [Type Constraints](references/type-constraints.md)\n126: - [ConstExpr Guide](references/constexpr-guide.md)\n\n(End of file - total 126 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\nname: pyasc-syntax-constraints\ndescription: pyasc Python syntax support and restrictions reference. Documents supported and unsupported Python syntax within @asc2.jit functions, type constraints, and ConstExpr usage. Trigger — when writing kernel code, checking if a Python construct is supported, or debugging JIT compilation errors related to syntax.\n---\n\n# pyasc Syntax Constraints\n\nSyntax and keyword support varies across v2 snapshots. For CANNBench, the\nsource of truth is `integrations/cannbench/pyasc-v2-source` at the commit in\n`SOURCE_COMMIT`; load `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` and verify uncertain constructs\nagainst that source plus the exact-v2 compile gate. In particular, its\n`asc2.range` supports `unroll_factor` and `gm_barrier`, but not `parallel`.\n\n## Overview\n\npyasc compiles Python code to Ascend C via JIT. Only a subset of Python syntax is supported inside `@asc2.jit`-decorated functions. This skill documents what is and is not allowed.\n\n## Supported Syntax\n\n| Syntax | Example | Notes |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/SKILL.md","text":"---\nname: pyasc-syntax-constraints\ndescription: pyasc Python syntax support and restrictions reference. Documents supported and unsupported Python syntax within @asc2.jit functions, type constraints, and ConstExpr usage. Trigger — when writing kernel code, checking if a Python construct is supported, or debugging JIT compilation errors related to syntax.\n---\n\n# pyasc Syntax Constraints\n\nSyntax and keyword support varies across v2 snapshots. For CANNBench, the\nsource of truth is `integrations/cannbench/pyasc-v2-source` at the commit in\n`SOURCE_COMMIT`; load `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` and verify uncertain constructs\nagainst that source plus the exact-v2 compile gate. In particular, its\n`asc2.range` supports `unroll_factor` and `gm_barrier`, but not `parallel`.\n\n## Overview\n\npyasc compiles Python code to Ascend C via JIT. Only a subset of Python syntax is supported inside `@asc2.jit`-decorated functions. This skill documents what is and is not allowed.\n\n## Supported Syntax\n\n| Syntax | Example | Notes |\n|--------|---------|-------|\n| Attribute access | `nums.__len__()` | |\n| `while` loop | `while i < n: ...` | |\n| `for` loop | `for i in asc2.range(n): ...` | Use `asc2.range()` inside kernel, not `range()` |\n| Binary operators | `a + b * c` | `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`, `//`, `**`, `&`, `\\|`, `^`, `<<`, `>>` |\n| Unary operators | `~a`, `-a`, `not a` | |\n| `tuple` | `return x, y, z` | |\n| `list` | `nums = [a, b, c]` | |\n| `pass` | `pass` | |\n| Ternary `if` | `ans = x if x > 0 else 0` | |\n| `if`/`elif`/`else` | Full conditional blocks | |\n| Constants | `a = 1; b = True` | |\n| Comparisons | `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `==`, `!=` | |\n| Function calls | `func()` | Must be `@asc2.jit`-decorated or asc2 built-in |\n| Boolean logic | `and`, `or` | |\n| Augmented assign | `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, `%=` | |\n| Assignment | `x = expr` | |\n| Annotated assign | `count: int = 3` | |\n| f-strings + assert | `assert cond, f\"msg {val}\"` | |\n| Subscript | `nums[0]` | |\n| Slice | `tensor[offset:]` | |\n\n## Unsupported Syntax\n\n| Syntax | Status | Workaround |\n|--------|--------|------------|\n| Nested functions | Not supported | Define separate `@asc2.jit` functions |\n| `global` | Not supported | Pass values as parameters |\n| `return` from kernel | Not supported | Kernels write to output tensors; device functions may return |\n| `return` inside `if`/`for` | Not supported | Use top-level return only in device functions |\n| `continue` | Not supported | Restructure loop logic |\n| `print()` | Not supported | Use `assert` with f-strings |\n| `with open(...)` | Not supported | Do file I/O outside JIT |\n| `raise` | Not supported | Use `assert` instead |\n| `try`/`except` | Not supported | Handle errors outside JIT |\n| `yield` / `yield from` | Not supported | No generators |\n| `lambda` | Not supported | Define named functions |\n| `break` | Not supported | Restructure loop logic |\n| `import` / `from...import` | Not supported | All imports outside JIT |\n| `async def` / `async with` | Not supported | No async |\n| `nonlocal` | Not supported | Pass values as parameters |\n| Class methods as kernels | Not supported | Use module-level functions |\n| If-scoped variables | Restricted | Initialize before `if`; use `asc.ConstExpr` for compile-time branching |\n| Unsigned int comparison | Restricted | Use `np.int64` or truthiness check instead |\n\n## Type Constraints\n\n### Kernel parameter types (runtime)\n\n| Supported | Not supported |\n|-----------|---------------|\n| `bool`, `int`, `float` | `str` |\n| `numpy` scalars and `ndarray` | `tuple`, `list`, `dict` |\n| `torch.Tensor` (NPU mode only) | Complex objects |\n| `asc.GlobalAddress` | |\n\n### Compile-time parameters\n\nUse `asc.ConstExpr[T]` for values that must be resolved at compile time:\n```python\n@asc2.jit(always_compile=True)\ndef kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    # tile_size is resolved at compile time and included in the JIT cache key\n    ...\n```\n\n### Built-in whitelist inside JIT\n\nOnly these built-ins are available: `dict`, `float`, `int`, `isinstance`, `issubclass`, `len`, `list`, `range`, `repr`, `str`, `tuple`, `type`\n\nNote: For iteration inside `@asc2.jit`, use `asc2.range()` instead of `range()`.\nDo not assume optional keywords are portable between pyasc snapshots.\n\n### Cube (matmul) loop + placement notes\n\n- **M/N/K tile loops are compile-time.** When the trip count is an\n  `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (matmul m/n/k tiles), a plain Python `for i in range(...)`\n  is fully unrolled at JIT time — that is the intended form for the loop that must\n  keep an operand resident in `L0A`/`L0B`. Use `asc2.range(...,\n  unroll_factor=2)` only on the *inner* tile loop you want software-pipelined\n  (double-buffered).\n- **Overlap (`gm_barrier=False`) doubles the pipelined L0 buffer.** The 2-deep\n  tile must fit half the L0 capacity (≤ 32 KiB for L0A/L0B, ≤ 64 KiB for the f32\n  L0C). A full-K `[256,128]` f16 L0B tile is 64 KiB and overflows when doubled\n  (`L0B overflow: 65536 bytes available, 131072 used`); shrink the tile (e.g.\n  `N_TILE=64`) before relying on overlap.\n- **Cube tile placement is explicit:** load/`asc2.copy` operands to\n  `asc2.TileLocation.L0A` (left) / `L0B` (right); stage from GM via\n  `asc2.TileLocation.L1` for reuse; the `@` result lands in L0C as f32 — cast with\n  `.to(asc2.float16)` before `asc2.store` if a 16-bit output is wanted.\n\n## Kernel vs Device Function Rules\n\n| Rule | Kernel function | Device function |\n|------|----------------|-----------------|\n| Launched from | Host via `kernel[core_num](...)` | Other `@asc2.jit` functions |\n| `return` value | Not allowed | Allowed |\n| `@asc2.jit(...)` options | Effective (always_compile, etc.) | Ignored |\n| Nesting | Cannot be nested | Cannot be nested |\n\n## References\n\n- [Supported Syntax Details](references/supported-syntax.md)\n- [Unsupported Syntax Details](references/unsupported-syntax.md)\n- [Type Constraints](references/type-constraints.md)\n- [ConstExpr Guide](references/constexpr-guide.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":126,"totalLines":126,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-syntax-constraints/SKILL.md","time":{"start":1788348498910,"end":1788348498914}},"id":"prt_061e082d1001r4UDX3X077hl62","sessionID":"ses_f9e20155cffePEnQZzaxI6Q8lc","messageID":"msg_061e056de001ESTATCpIszd2Xe"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788348499268,"sessionID":"ses_f9e20155cffePEnQZzaxI6Q8lc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_6dc63bc93a5f4a708da7a80b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/local_compile_gate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/local_compile_gate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\n2: \"\"\"Compile every CANNBench case dispatch against the submitted pyasc v2 runtime.\n3: \n4: The gate runs in the amd64/QEMU image built by ``run_local_compile_gate.sh``.\n5: It imports an operator module with a tiny fake ``torch`` host API, records the\n6: JIT launches selected by each benchmark case, and lowers every unique launch\n7: specialization through pyasc to generated AscendC.  No CANNBench credit, NPU,\n8: or torch installation is required.\n9: \n10: This proves host dispatch, pyasc AST/codegen, compiler passes, translation, and\n11: the 950PR UB budget.  It deliberately does not claim numerical correctness or\n12: silicon performance; those remain camodel/NPU and CANNBench responsibilities.\n13: \"\"\"\n14: \n15: from __future__ import annotations\n16: \n17: import argparse\n18: import importlib.util\n19: import inspect\n20: import json\n21: import math\n22: import os\n23: import sys\n24: import types\n25: from dataclasses import dataclass\n26: from pathlib import Path\n27: from typing import Any\n28: \n29: import yaml\n30: \n31: \n32: PYASC_COMMIT = \"ac1222a48c8914d3f81297c7570d1a84f0f26778\"\n33: PLATFORM = \"Ascend950PR_9599\"\n34: \n35: \n36: @dataclass(frozen=True)\n37: class FakeDType:\n38:     name: str\n39:     itemsize: int\n40: \n41:     def __str__(self) -> str:\n42:         return f\"torch.{self.name}\"\n43: \n44: \n45: DTYPES = {\n46:     \"float16\": FakeDType(\"float16\", 2),\n47:     \"bfloat16\": FakeDType(\"bfloat16\", 2),\n48:     \"float32\": FakeDType(\"float32\", 4),\n49:     \"int8\": FakeDType(\"int8\", 1),\n50:     \"uint8\": FakeDType(\"uint8\", 1),\n51:     \"int16\": FakeDType(\"int16\", 2),\n52:     \"int32\": FakeDType(\"int32\", 4),\n53:     \"int64\": FakeDType(\"int64\", 8),\n54:     \"bool\": FakeDType(\"bool\", 1),\n55: }\n56: \n57: \n58: class FakeTensor:\n59:     \"\"\"Shape/dtype-only tensor sufficient for CANNBench host dispatch.\"\"\"\n60: \n61:     def __init__(self, shape: Any, dtype: FakeDType, device: str = \"npu:0\"):\n62:         if isinstance(shape, int):\n63:             shape = (shape,)\n64:         self.shape = tuple(int(v) for v in shape)\n65:         self.dtype = dtype\n66:         self.device = device\n67: \n68:     @property\n69:     def ndim(self) -> int:\n70:         return len(self.shape)\n71: \n72:     def dim(self) -> int:\n73:         return self.ndim\n74: \n75:     def numel(self) -> int:\n76:         return math.prod(self.shape)\n77: \n78:     def element_size(self) -> int:\n79:         return self.dtype.itemsize\n80: \n81:     def is_contiguous(self) -> bool:\n82:         return True\n83: \n84:     def contiguous(self) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n85:         return self\n86: \n87:     def size(self, dim: int | None = None):\n88:         return self.shape if dim is None else self.shape[dim]\n89: \n90:     def narrow(self, dim: int, start: int, length: int) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n91:         del start\n92:         shape = list(self.shape)\n93:         shape[dim] = int(length)\n94:         return FakeTensor(shape, self.dtype, self.device)\n95: \n96:     def view(self, *args: Any) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n97:         if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], FakeDType):\n98:             return FakeTensor(self.shape, args[0], self.device)\n99:         return self.reshape(*args)\n100: \n101:     def reshape(self, *args: Any) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n102:         if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], (list, tuple)):\n103:             args = tuple(args[0])\n104:         shape = [int(v) for v in args]\n105:         if shape.count(-1) > 1:\n106:             raise ValueError(\"only one inferred dimension is supported\")\n107:         if -1 in shape:\n108:             idx = shape.index(-1)\n109:             known = math.prod(v for v in shape if v != -1)\n110:             shape[idx] = self.numel() // known\n111:         return FakeTensor(shape, self.dtype, self.device)\n112: \n113:     def flatten(self) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n114:         return FakeTensor((self.numel(),), self.dtype, self.device)\n115: \n116:     def __len__(self) -> int:\n117:         return self.shape[0]\n118: \n119:     def __getitem__(self, key: Any) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n120:         if isinstance(key, int):\n121:             return FakeTensor(self.shape[1:], self.dtype, self.device)\n122:         return self\n123: \n124: \n125: class FakeTorch(types.ModuleType):\n126:     def __init__(self) -> None:\n127:         super().__init__(\"torch\")\n128:         self.Tensor = FakeTensor\n129:         for name, dtype in DTYPES.items():\n130:             setattr(self, name, dtype)\n131:         self.half = DTYPES[\"float16\"]\n132:         self.float = DTYPES[\"float32\"]\n133: \n134:     @staticmethod\n135:     def _shape(args: tuple[Any, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n136:         if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], int):\n137:             return (args[0],)\n138:         if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], (list, tuple)):\n139:             return tuple(args[0])\n140:         return tuple(args)\n141: \n142:     def empty(self, *shape: Any, dtype=None, device=None, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n143:         return FakeTensor(self._shape(shape), dtype or self.float32, device or \"npu:0\")\n144: \n145:     def zeros(self, *shape: Any, dtype=None, device=None, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n146:         return self.empty(*shape, dtype=dtype, device=device)\n147: \n148:     def tensor(self, value: Any, dtype=None, device=None, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n149:         shape = () if not isinstance(value, (list, tuple)) else (len(value),)\n150:         return FakeTensor(shape, dtype or self.float32, device or \"npu:0\")\n151: \n152:     @staticmethod\n153:     def empty_like(tensor: FakeTensor, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n154:         return FakeTensor(tensor.shape, tensor.dtype, tensor.device)\n155: \n156:     @staticmethod\n157:     def zeros_like(tensor: FakeTensor, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n158:         return FakeTensor(tensor.shape, tensor.dtype, tensor.device)\n159: \n160: \n161: @dataclass\n162: class Launch:\n163:     case_id: int\n164:     kernel_name: str\n165:     jit: Any\n166:     cores: Any\n167:     args: tuple[Any, ...]\n168:     specialization: str | None = None\n169: \n170: \n171: class CaptureKernel:\n172:     def __init__(self, case_id: int, name: str, jit: Any,\n173:                  launches: list[Launch], failed_specializations: set[str]):\n174:         self.case_id = case_id\n175:         self.name = name\n176:         self.jit = jit\n177:         self.launches = launches\n178:         self.failed_specializations = failed_specializations\n179: \n180:     def __getitem__(self, cores: Any):\n181:         def record(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n182:             if kwargs:\n183:                 raise TypeError(\"keyword JIT launch arguments are not supported by the local gate\")\n184:             launch = Launch(self.case_id, self.name, self.jit, cores, args)\n185:             try:\n186:                 launch.specialization = prepare_specialization(self.jit, args)[0]\n187:             except Exception as exc:\n188:                 launch.specialization = (\n189:                     f\"prepare-error:{self.name}:{type(exc).__name__}:{exc}\"\n190:                 )\n191:             self.launches.append(launch)\n192:             # On a repeated dispatch, reproduce a known compile-time exception.\n193:             # This lets host-side try/fallback logic (for example GELU's wide\n194:             # tile -> safe tile route) select the same path as a real launch.\n195:             if launch.specialization in self.failed_specializations:\n196:                 raise RuntimeError(\n197:                     f\"local compile gate rejected {launch.specialization}\"\n198:                 )\n199:         return record\n200: \n201: \n202: def tensor(shape: Any, dtype: str) -> FakeTensor:\n203:     return FakeTensor(shape, DTYPES[dtype])\n204: \n205: \n206: def case_call(op: str, fn: Any, case: dict[str, Any]) -> Any:\n207:     shapes = case[\"input_shape\"]\n208:     dtypes = case[\"dtype\"]\n209:     attrs = case.get(\"attrs\") or {}\n210:     if op in {\"sigmoid\", \"exp\", \"mish\", \"gelu\"}:\n211:         return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), **attrs)\n212:     if op == \"masked_scale\":\n213:         return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), tensor(shapes[1], dtypes[1]), **attrs)\n214:     if op == \"swi_glu\":\n215:         return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), **attrs)\n216:     if op == \"rms_norm\":\n217:         return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), tensor(shapes[1], dtypes[1]), **attrs)\n218:     if op == \"foreach_norm\":\n219:         xs = [tensor(shape, dtypes[0]) for shape in shapes[0]]\n220:         return fn(xs, **attrs)\n221:     if op == \"foreach_addcdiv_scalar\":\n222:         lists = [[tensor(shape, dtypes[0]) for shape in group] for group in shapes]\n223:         return fn(*lists, **attrs)\n224:     raise ValueError(f\"unsupported operator {op!r}\")\n225: \n226: \n227: def load_candidate(path: Path, op: str):\n228:     fake_torch = FakeTorch()\n229:     sys.modules[\"torch\"] = fake_torch\n230:     package_name = \"_local_cann_bench_candidate\"\n231:     package = types.ModuleType(package_name)\n232:     package.__path__ = [str(path.parent)]\n233:     sys.modules[package_name] = package\n234:     runtime = types.ModuleType(f\"{package_name}._pyasc_runtime\")\n235:     runtime.ensure_npu_platform = lambda: None\n236:     sys.modules[runtime.__name__] = runtime\n237:     spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(f\"{package_name}.{op}\", path)\n238:     if spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n239:         raise RuntimeError(f\"cannot import {path}\")\n240:     module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n241:     sys.modules[spec.name] = module\n242:     spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n243:     module.torch = fake_torch\n244:     return module\n245: \n246: \n247: def mock_arg(value: Any):\n248:     from asc import DataType\n249:     from asc.runtime.jit import MockTensor\n250: \n251:     if isinstance(value, FakeTensor):\n252:         return MockTensor(DataType(value.dtype.name))\n253:     return value\n254: \n255: \n256: def prepare_specialization(jit: Any, args: tuple[Any, ...]):\n257:     from asc.common.compat import get_annotations, merge_dict\n258: \n259:     kwargs = merge_dict(jit.default_options, {})\n260:     codegen_options = jit.extract_kwargs(jit.codegen.options_cls, kwargs)\n261:     compile_options = jit.extract_kwargs(jit.compiler.options_cls, kwargs)\n262:     mocked = tuple(mock_arg(arg) for arg in args)\n263:     call_args = inspect.signature(jit.fn).bind(*mocked).arguments\n264:     runtime_args, constexprs = jit.split_args(call_args, get_annotations(jit.fn))\n265:     arg_types = {name: jit.get_arg_type(value) for name, value in runtime_args.items()}\n266:     key_data = {\n267:         \"kernel\": jit.fn.__name__,\n268:         \"arg_types\": {name: f\"{type(value).__name__}:{jit.get_arg_dtype(value)}\"\n269:                       for name, value in arg_types.items()},\n270:         \"constexprs\": {name: repr(value) for name, value in constexprs.items()},\n271:         \"codegen\": vars(codegen_options),\n272:         \"compile\": vars(compile_options),\n273:     }\n274:     key = json.dumps(key_data, sort_keys=True, default=str)\n275:     return key, arg_types, constexprs, codegen_options, compile_options\n276: \n277: \n278: def compile_specialization(jit: Any, prepared: tuple[Any, ...]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n279:     from asc._C import ir\n280:     from asc.codegen.specialization import Specialization\n281: \n282:     _, arg_types, constexprs, codegen_options, compile_options = prepared\n283:     module = jit._run_codegen(Specialization(arg_types, constexprs), codegen_options)\n284:     # Use the compiler class bound to this JIT object. asc2.JITFunction binds\n285:     # asc2.runtime.compiler.Compiler; using asc.runtime.Compiler here silently\n286:     # skips the AscTile lowering pipeline and leaves local tensors untranslated.\n287:     compiler = jit.compiler(compile_options)\n288:     compiler.preprocess_module(module)\n289:     if compile_options.run_passes:\n290:         compiler.run_passes(module)\n291:     compiler.postprocess_module(module)\n292:     source = compiler.run_translation(module)\n293:     memory = module.op.get_dict_of_int_attr(ir.attr.memory_consumed)\n294:     jit.launcher.check_memory_overflow(memory)\n295:     return {\n296:         \"status\": \"passed\",\n297:         \"memory_consumed\": memory,\n298:         \"ascendc_bytes\": len(source.encode(\"utf-8\")),\n299:     }\n300: \n301: \n302: def evaluate(candidate: Path, op: str, cases_path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n303:     import asc.runtime.config as config\n304:     from asc.runtime.jit import JITFunction\n305: \n306:     os.environ.setdefault(\"PYASC_COMPILER\", \"/bin/true\")\n307:     os.environ.setdefault(\"PYASC_LINKER\", \"/bin/true\")\n308:     config.set_platform(config.Backend.Model, config.Platform(PLATFORM), check=False)\n309: \n310:     module = load_candidate(candidate, op)\n311:     fn = getattr(module, op)\n312:     originals = {\n313:         name: value for name, value in vars(module).items()\n314:         if isinstance(value, JITFunction)\n315:     }\n316:     cases = yaml.safe_load(cases_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"cases\"]\n317:     launches: list[Launch] = []\n318:     case_results: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n319:     compiled: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n320:     failed_specializations: set[str] = set()\n321: \n322:     for case in cases:\n323:         case_id = int(case[\"case_id\"])\n324:         final_launches: list[Launch] = []\n325:         dispatch_error: str | None = None\n326:         # First pass discovers the optimistic route. If that route fails to\n327:         # compile, subsequent passes inject the failure back into the wrapper\n328:         # so explicit host fallback code can execute.\n329:         for _attempt in range(3):\n330:             selected: list[Launch] = []\n331:             for name, jit in originals.items():\n332:                 setattr(\n333:                     module, name,\n334:                     CaptureKernel(\n335:                         case_id, name, jit, selected, failed_specializations\n336:                     ),\n337:                 )\n338:             try:\n339:                 case_call(op, fn, case)\n340:                 dispatch_error = None\n341:             except Exception as exc:\n342:                 dispatch_error = f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n343:             finally:\n344:                 for name, jit in originals.items():\n345:                     setattr(module, name, jit)\n346:             launches.extend(selected)\n347:             final_launches = selected\n348: \n349:             discovered_failure = False\n350:             for launch in selected:\n351:                 key = launch.specialization\n352:                 if key in compiled:\n353:                     continue\n354:                 try:\n355:                     prepared = prepare_specialization(launch.jit, launch.args)\n356:                     compiled[key] = compile_specialization(launch.jit, prepared)\n357:                 except Exception as exc:\n358:                     compiled[key] = {\n359:                         \"status\": \"failed\",\n360:                         \"error\": f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\",\n361:                     }\n362:                     failed_specializations.add(key)\n363:                     discovered_failure = True\n364:             if discovered_failure:\n365:                 continue\n366:             break\n367: \n368:         successful = [\n369:             launch for launch in final_launches\n370:             if compiled.get(launch.specialization, {}).get(\"status\") == \"passed\"\n371:         ]\n372:         failed = [\n373:             compiled[launch.specialization] for launch in final_launches\n374:             if compiled.get(launch.specialization, {}).get(\"status\") != \"passed\"\n375:         ]\n376:         if dispatch_error is not None or not successful:\n377:             case_results.append({\n378:                 \"case_id\": case_id,\n379:                 \"dispatch\": \"failed\" if dispatch_error else \"passed\",\n380:                 \"compile\": \"failed\",\n381:                 \"error\": dispatch_error,\n382:                 \"compile_errors\": sorted({item.get(\"error\", \"unknown\") for item in failed}),\n383:                 \"kernels\": [launch.kernel_name for launch in final_launches],\n384:                 \"cores\": [launch.cores for launch in final_launches],\n385:             })\n386:             continue\n387:         case_results.append({\n388:             \"case_id\": case_id,\n389:             \"dispatch\": \"passed\",\n390:             \"compile\": \"passed\",\n391:             \"kernels\": [launch.kernel_name for launch in successful],\n392:             \"cores\": [launch.cores for launch in successful],\n393:             \"handled_compile_failures\": sorted({\n394:                 item.get(\"error\", \"unknown\") for item in failed\n395:             }),\n396:         })\n397: \n398:     dispatch_passed = sum(item[\"dispatch\"] == \"passed\" for item in case_results)\n399:     compile_passed = sum(item.get(\"compile\") == \"passed\" for item in case_results)\n400:     unique_passed = sum(item[\"status\"] == \"passed\" for item in compiled.values())\n401:     report = {\n402:         \"schema_version\": 1,\n403:         \"operator\": op,\n404:         \"candidate\": str(candidate),\n405:         \"pyasc_source\": \"https://gitcode.com/compiler-team/pyasc/tree/v2\",\n406:         \"pyasc_commit\": PYASC_COMMIT,\n407:         \"runtime\": \"self-contained CANNBench wheel with repository overlays\",\n408:         \"platform\": PLATFORM,\n409:         \"method\": \"QEMU host dispatch + pyasc codegen/passes/AscendC translation\",\n410:         \"limitations\": [\n411:             \"does not execute numerical code\",\n412:             \"does not estimate camodel ticks or NPU performance\",\n413:             \"CANNBench remains the acceptance oracle when submissions are available\",\n414:         ],\n415:         \"cases\": len(cases),\n416:         \"dispatch_passed\": dispatch_passed,\n417:         \"compile_passed\": compile_passed,\n418:         \"unique_specializations\": len(compiled),\n419:         \"unique_specializations_passed\": unique_passed,\n420:         \"status\": \"passed\" if dispatch_passed == len(cases)\n421:                   and compile_passed == len(cases) else \"failed\",\n422:         \"case_results\": case_results,\n423:         \"specializations\": list(compiled.values()),\n424:     }\n425:     return report\n426: \n427: \n428: def main() -> int:\n429:     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n430:     parser.add_argument(\"--candidate\", required=True, type=Path)\n431:     parser.add_argument(\"--op\", required=True)\n432:     parser.add_argument(\"--cases\", type=Path)\n433:     parser.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path)\n434:     args = parser.parse_args()\n435:     cases = args.cases or Path(\"integrations/cannbench/tasks\") / args.op / \"cases.yaml\"\n436:     try:\n437:         report = evaluate(args.candidate, args.op, cases)\n438:     except Exception as exc:\n439:         report = {\n440:             \"schema_version\": 1,\n441:             \"operator\": args.op,\n442:             \"candidate\": str(args.candidate),\n443:             \"pyasc_commit\": PYASC_COMMIT,\n444:             \"platform\": PLATFORM,\n445:             \"status\": \"failed\",\n446:             \"fatal_error\": f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\",\n447:         }\n448:     payload = json.dumps(report, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n449:     if args.output:\n450:         args.output.write_text(payload + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n451:     print(payload)\n452:     return 0 if report[\"status\"] == \"passed\" else 1\n453: \n454: \n455: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n456:     raise SystemExit(main())\n\n(End of file - total 456 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Compile every CANNBench case dispatch against the submitted pyasc v2 runtime.\n\nThe gate runs in the amd64/QEMU image built by ``run_local_compile_gate.sh``.\nIt imports an operator module with a tiny fake ``torch`` host API, records the\nJIT launches selected by each benchmark case, and lowers every unique launch\nspecialization through pyasc to generated AscendC.  No CANNBench credit, NPU,\nor torch installation is required.\n\nThis proves host dispatch, pyasc AST/codegen, compiler passes, translation, and\nthe 950PR UB budget.  It deliberately does not claim numerical correctness or\nsilicon performance; those remain camodel/NPU and CANNBench responsibilities.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport importlib.util\nimport inspect\nimport json","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/local_compile_gate.py","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Compile every CANNBench case dispatch against the submitted pyasc v2 runtime.\n\nThe gate runs in the amd64/QEMU image built by ``run_local_compile_gate.sh``.\nIt imports an operator module with a tiny fake ``torch`` host API, records the\nJIT launches selected by each benchmark case, and lowers every unique launch\nspecialization through pyasc to generated AscendC.  No CANNBench credit, NPU,\nor torch installation is required.\n\nThis proves host dispatch, pyasc AST/codegen, compiler passes, translation, and\nthe 950PR UB budget.  It deliberately does not claim numerical correctness or\nsilicon performance; those remain camodel/NPU and CANNBench responsibilities.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport importlib.util\nimport inspect\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport types\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport yaml\n\n\nPYASC_COMMIT = \"ac1222a48c8914d3f81297c7570d1a84f0f26778\"\nPLATFORM = \"Ascend950PR_9599\"\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FakeDType:\n    name: str\n    itemsize: int\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        return f\"torch.{self.name}\"\n\n\nDTYPES = {\n    \"float16\": FakeDType(\"float16\", 2),\n    \"bfloat16\": FakeDType(\"bfloat16\", 2),\n    \"float32\": FakeDType(\"float32\", 4),\n    \"int8\": FakeDType(\"int8\", 1),\n    \"uint8\": FakeDType(\"uint8\", 1),\n    \"int16\": FakeDType(\"int16\", 2),\n    \"int32\": FakeDType(\"int32\", 4),\n    \"int64\": FakeDType(\"int64\", 8),\n    \"bool\": FakeDType(\"bool\", 1),\n}\n\n\nclass FakeTensor:\n    \"\"\"Shape/dtype-only tensor sufficient for CANNBench host dispatch.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, shape: Any, dtype: FakeDType, device: str = \"npu:0\"):\n        if isinstance(shape, int):\n            shape = (shape,)\n        self.shape = tuple(int(v) for v in shape)\n        self.dtype = dtype\n        self.device = device\n\n    @property\n    def ndim(self) -> int:\n        return len(self.shape)\n\n    def dim(self) -> int:\n        return self.ndim\n\n    def numel(self) -> int:\n        return math.prod(self.shape)\n\n    def element_size(self) -> int:\n        return self.dtype.itemsize\n\n    def is_contiguous(self) -> bool:\n        return True\n\n    def contiguous(self) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n        return self\n\n    def size(self, dim: int | None = None):\n        return self.shape if dim is None else self.shape[dim]\n\n    def narrow(self, dim: int, start: int, length: int) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n        del start\n        shape = list(self.shape)\n        shape[dim] = int(length)\n        return FakeTensor(shape, self.dtype, self.device)\n\n    def view(self, *args: Any) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n        if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], FakeDType):\n            return FakeTensor(self.shape, args[0], self.device)\n        return self.reshape(*args)\n\n    def reshape(self, *args: Any) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n        if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], (list, tuple)):\n            args = tuple(args[0])\n        shape = [int(v) for v in args]\n        if shape.count(-1) > 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"only one inferred dimension is supported\")\n        if -1 in shape:\n            idx = shape.index(-1)\n            known = math.prod(v for v in shape if v != -1)\n            shape[idx] = self.numel() // known\n        return FakeTensor(shape, self.dtype, self.device)\n\n    def flatten(self) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n        return FakeTensor((self.numel(),), self.dtype, self.device)\n\n    def __len__(self) -> int:\n        return self.shape[0]\n\n    def __getitem__(self, key: Any) -> \"FakeTensor\":\n        if isinstance(key, int):\n            return FakeTensor(self.shape[1:], self.dtype, self.device)\n        return self\n\n\nclass FakeTorch(types.ModuleType):\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\"torch\")\n        self.Tensor = FakeTensor\n        for name, dtype in DTYPES.items():\n            setattr(self, name, dtype)\n        self.half = DTYPES[\"float16\"]\n        self.float = DTYPES[\"float32\"]\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _shape(args: tuple[Any, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n        if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], int):\n            return (args[0],)\n        if len(args) == 1 and isinstance(args[0], (list, tuple)):\n            return tuple(args[0])\n        return tuple(args)\n\n    def empty(self, *shape: Any, dtype=None, device=None, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n        return FakeTensor(self._shape(shape), dtype or self.float32, device or \"npu:0\")\n\n    def zeros(self, *shape: Any, dtype=None, device=None, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n        return self.empty(*shape, dtype=dtype, device=device)\n\n    def tensor(self, value: Any, dtype=None, device=None, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n        shape = () if not isinstance(value, (list, tuple)) else (len(value),)\n        return FakeTensor(shape, dtype or self.float32, device or \"npu:0\")\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def empty_like(tensor: FakeTensor, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n        return FakeTensor(tensor.shape, tensor.dtype, tensor.device)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def zeros_like(tensor: FakeTensor, **_: Any) -> FakeTensor:\n        return FakeTensor(tensor.shape, tensor.dtype, tensor.device)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Launch:\n    case_id: int\n    kernel_name: str\n    jit: Any\n    cores: Any\n    args: tuple[Any, ...]\n    specialization: str | None = None\n\n\nclass CaptureKernel:\n    def __init__(self, case_id: int, name: str, jit: Any,\n                 launches: list[Launch], failed_specializations: set[str]):\n        self.case_id = case_id\n        self.name = name\n        self.jit = jit\n        self.launches = launches\n        self.failed_specializations = failed_specializations\n\n    def __getitem__(self, cores: Any):\n        def record(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n            if kwargs:\n                raise TypeError(\"keyword JIT launch arguments are not supported by the local gate\")\n            launch = Launch(self.case_id, self.name, self.jit, cores, args)\n            try:\n                launch.specialization = prepare_specialization(self.jit, args)[0]\n            except Exception as exc:\n                launch.specialization = (\n                    f\"prepare-error:{self.name}:{type(exc).__name__}:{exc}\"\n                )\n            self.launches.append(launch)\n            # On a repeated dispatch, reproduce a known compile-time exception.\n            # This lets host-side try/fallback logic (for example GELU's wide\n            # tile -> safe tile route) select the same path as a real launch.\n            if launch.specialization in self.failed_specializations:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    f\"local compile gate rejected {launch.specialization}\"\n                )\n        return record\n\n\ndef tensor(shape: Any, dtype: str) -> FakeTensor:\n    return FakeTensor(shape, DTYPES[dtype])\n\n\ndef case_call(op: str, fn: Any, case: dict[str, Any]) -> Any:\n    shapes = case[\"input_shape\"]\n    dtypes = case[\"dtype\"]\n    attrs = case.get(\"attrs\") or {}\n    if op in {\"sigmoid\", \"exp\", \"mish\", \"gelu\"}:\n        return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), **attrs)\n    if op == \"masked_scale\":\n        return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), tensor(shapes[1], dtypes[1]), **attrs)\n    if op == \"swi_glu\":\n        return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), **attrs)\n    if op == \"rms_norm\":\n        return fn(tensor(shapes[0], dtypes[0]), tensor(shapes[1], dtypes[1]), **attrs)\n    if op == \"foreach_norm\":\n        xs = [tensor(shape, dtypes[0]) for shape in shapes[0]]\n        return fn(xs, **attrs)\n    if op == \"foreach_addcdiv_scalar\":\n        lists = [[tensor(shape, dtypes[0]) for shape in group] for group in shapes]\n        return fn(*lists, **attrs)\n    raise ValueError(f\"unsupported operator {op!r}\")\n\n\ndef load_candidate(path: Path, op: str):\n    fake_torch = FakeTorch()\n    sys.modules[\"torch\"] = fake_torch\n    package_name = \"_local_cann_bench_candidate\"\n    package = types.ModuleType(package_name)\n    package.__path__ = [str(path.parent)]\n    sys.modules[package_name] = package\n    runtime = types.ModuleType(f\"{package_name}._pyasc_runtime\")\n    runtime.ensure_npu_platform = lambda: None\n    sys.modules[runtime.__name__] = runtime\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(f\"{package_name}.{op}\", path)\n    if spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"cannot import {path}\")\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    sys.modules[spec.name] = module\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    module.torch = fake_torch\n    return module\n\n\ndef mock_arg(value: Any):\n    from asc import DataType\n    from asc.runtime.jit import MockTensor\n\n    if isinstance(value, FakeTensor):\n        return MockTensor(DataType(value.dtype.name))\n    return value\n\n\ndef prepare_specialization(jit: Any, args: tuple[Any, ...]):\n    from asc.common.compat import get_annotations, merge_dict\n\n    kwargs = merge_dict(jit.default_options, {})\n    codegen_options = jit.extract_kwargs(jit.codegen.options_cls, kwargs)\n    compile_options = jit.extract_kwargs(jit.compiler.options_cls, kwargs)\n    mocked = tuple(mock_arg(arg) for arg in args)\n    call_args = inspect.signature(jit.fn).bind(*mocked).arguments\n    runtime_args, constexprs = jit.split_args(call_args, get_annotations(jit.fn))\n    arg_types = {name: jit.get_arg_type(value) for name, value in runtime_args.items()}\n    key_data = {\n        \"kernel\": jit.fn.__name__,\n        \"arg_types\": {name: f\"{type(value).__name__}:{jit.get_arg_dtype(value)}\"\n                      for name, value in arg_types.items()},\n        \"constexprs\": {name: repr(value) for name, value in constexprs.items()},\n        \"codegen\": vars(codegen_options),\n        \"compile\": vars(compile_options),\n    }\n    key = json.dumps(key_data, sort_keys=True, default=str)\n    return key, arg_types, constexprs, codegen_options, compile_options\n\n\ndef compile_specialization(jit: Any, prepared: tuple[Any, ...]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    from asc._C import ir\n    from asc.codegen.specialization import Specialization\n\n    _, arg_types, constexprs, codegen_options, compile_options = prepared\n    module = jit._run_codegen(Specialization(arg_types, constexprs), codegen_options)\n    # Use the compiler class bound to this JIT object. asc2.JITFunction binds\n    # asc2.runtime.compiler.Compiler; using asc.runtime.Compiler here silently\n    # skips the AscTile lowering pipeline and leaves local tensors untranslated.\n    compiler = jit.compiler(compile_options)\n    compiler.preprocess_module(module)\n    if compile_options.run_passes:\n        compiler.run_passes(module)\n    compiler.postprocess_module(module)\n    source = compiler.run_translation(module)\n    memory = module.op.get_dict_of_int_attr(ir.attr.memory_consumed)\n    jit.launcher.check_memory_overflow(memory)\n    return {\n        \"status\": \"passed\",\n        \"memory_consumed\": memory,\n        \"ascendc_bytes\": len(source.encode(\"utf-8\")),\n    }\n\n\ndef evaluate(candidate: Path, op: str, cases_path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    import asc.runtime.config as config\n    from asc.runtime.jit import JITFunction\n\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PYASC_COMPILER\", \"/bin/true\")\n    os.environ.setdefault(\"PYASC_LINKER\", \"/bin/true\")\n    config.set_platform(config.Backend.Model, config.Platform(PLATFORM), check=False)\n\n    module = load_candidate(candidate, op)\n    fn = getattr(module, op)\n    originals = {\n        name: value for name, value in vars(module).items()\n        if isinstance(value, JITFunction)\n    }\n    cases = yaml.safe_load(cases_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"cases\"]\n    launches: list[Launch] = []\n    case_results: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    compiled: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    failed_specializations: set[str] = set()\n\n    for case in cases:\n        case_id = int(case[\"case_id\"])\n        final_launches: list[Launch] = []\n        dispatch_error: str | None = None\n        # First pass discovers the optimistic route. If that route fails to\n        # compile, subsequent passes inject the failure back into the wrapper\n        # so explicit host fallback code can execute.\n        for _attempt in range(3):\n            selected: list[Launch] = []\n            for name, jit in originals.items():\n                setattr(\n                    module, name,\n                    CaptureKernel(\n                        case_id, name, jit, selected, failed_specializations\n                    ),\n                )\n            try:\n                case_call(op, fn, case)\n                dispatch_error = None\n            except Exception as exc:\n                dispatch_error = f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n            finally:\n                for name, jit in originals.items():\n                    setattr(module, name, jit)\n            launches.extend(selected)\n            final_launches = selected\n\n            discovered_failure = False\n            for launch in selected:\n                key = launch.specialization\n                if key in compiled:\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    prepared = prepare_specialization(launch.jit, launch.args)\n                    compiled[key] = compile_specialization(launch.jit, prepared)\n                except Exception as exc:\n                    compiled[key] = {\n                        \"status\": \"failed\",\n                        \"error\": f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\",\n                    }\n                    failed_specializations.add(key)\n                    discovered_failure = True\n            if discovered_failure:\n                continue\n            break\n\n        successful = [\n            launch for launch in final_launches\n            if compiled.get(launch.specialization, {}).get(\"status\") == \"passed\"\n        ]\n        failed = [\n            compiled[launch.specialization] for launch in final_launches\n            if compiled.get(launch.specialization, {}).get(\"status\") != \"passed\"\n        ]\n        if dispatch_error is not None or not successful:\n            case_results.append({\n                \"case_id\": case_id,\n                \"dispatch\": \"failed\" if dispatch_error else \"passed\",\n                \"compile\": \"failed\",\n                \"error\": dispatch_error,\n                \"compile_errors\": sorted({item.get(\"error\", \"unknown\") for item in failed}),\n                \"kernels\": [launch.kernel_name for launch in final_launches],\n                \"cores\": [launch.cores for launch in final_launches],\n            })\n            continue\n        case_results.append({\n            \"case_id\": case_id,\n            \"dispatch\": \"passed\",\n            \"compile\": \"passed\",\n            \"kernels\": [launch.kernel_name for launch in successful],\n            \"cores\": [launch.cores for launch in successful],\n            \"handled_compile_failures\": sorted({\n                item.get(\"error\", \"unknown\") for item in failed\n            }),\n        })\n\n    dispatch_passed = sum(item[\"dispatch\"] == \"passed\" for item in case_results)\n    compile_passed = sum(item.get(\"compile\") == \"passed\" for item in case_results)\n    unique_passed = sum(item[\"status\"] == \"passed\" for item in compiled.values())\n    report = {\n        \"schema_version\": 1,\n        \"operator\": op,\n        \"candidate\": str(candidate),\n        \"pyasc_source\": \"https://gitcode.com/compiler-team/pyasc/tree/v2\",\n        \"pyasc_commit\": PYASC_COMMIT,\n        \"runtime\": \"self-contained CANNBench wheel with repository overlays\",\n        \"platform\": PLATFORM,\n        \"method\": \"QEMU host dispatch + pyasc codegen/passes/AscendC translation\",\n        \"limitations\": [\n            \"does not execute numerical code\",\n            \"does not estimate camodel ticks or NPU performance\",\n            \"CANNBench remains the acceptance oracle when submissions are available\",\n        ],\n        \"cases\": len(cases),\n        \"dispatch_passed\": dispatch_passed,\n        \"compile_passed\": compile_passed,\n        \"unique_specializations\": len(compiled),\n        \"unique_specializations_passed\": unique_passed,\n        \"status\": \"passed\" if dispatch_passed == len(cases)\n                  and compile_passed == len(cases) else \"failed\",\n        \"case_results\": case_results,\n        \"specializations\": list(compiled.values()),\n    }\n    return report\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"--candidate\", required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--op\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--cases\", type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    cases = args.cases or Path(\"integrations/cannbench/tasks\") / args.op / \"cases.yaml\"\n    try:\n        report = evaluate(args.candidate, args.op, cases)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        report = {\n            \"schema_version\": 1,\n            \"operator\": args.op,\n            \"candidate\": str(args.candidate),\n            \"pyasc_commit\": PYASC_COMMIT,\n            \"platform\": PLATFORM,\n            \"status\": \"failed\",\n            \"fatal_error\": f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\",\n        }\n    payload = json.dumps(report, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n    if args.output:\n        args.output.write_text(payload + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(payload)\n    return 0 if report[\"status\"] == \"passed\" else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":456,"totalLines":456,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/local_compile_gate.py","time":{"start":1788348499263,"end":1788348499267}},"id":"prt_061e083f3001Dpd3kaXFWhNw5e","sessionID":"ses_f9e20155cffePEnQZzaxI6Q8lc","messageID":"msg_061e056de001ESTATCpIszd2Xe"}}
