{"type":"text","timestamp":1788348692187,"sessionID":"ses_f9e20155cffePEnQZzaxI6Q8lc","part":{"id":"prt_061e340310018FgOpDgyN9btHT","messageID":"msg_061e0ba2f001pr41USAmdKXaCT","sessionID":"ses_f9e20155cffePEnQZzaxI6Q8lc","type":"text","text":"I have read all three files and the skill references. Now let me systematically review the candidate against the CANNBench contract and all 20 case routes.\n\n## Static Review\n\n**1. Module shape** (contract §Module shape)\n- Imports: `torch`, `asc`, `asc2`, `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` ✓\n- One `@asc2.jit` kernel `_addcdiv_kernel` ✓\n- Public callable `foreach_addcdiv_scalar` with exact schema signature ✓\n- `ensure_npu_platform()` called first ✓\n- `torch.empty_like(a)` for output allocation ✓\n- Launch `kernel[cores](...)` with no stream arg ✓\n\n**2. Pinned-v2 API correctness**\n- `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` — 1-D ✓ (not `asc2.tensor`/`asc.GlobalTensor`)\n- `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` ✓\n- `asc2.copy_out(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` ✓\n- Ranks consistent (all 1-D) ✓\n\n**3. Kernel signature**\n- Pointers: `asc.GlobalAddress` ✓; sizes: plain `int` ✓; scalar: `float` ✓; tile_size: `asc.ConstExpr[int]` ✓\n\n**4. Grid-stride loop**\n- `asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2)` ✓\n- Only `unroll_factor` kwarg (no unsupported `parallel`/`gm_barrier`) ✓\n- Tail: `n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off` ✓\n\n**5. Numerical correctness vs golden**\n- f16/bf16 promoted to f32 via `.to(asc.float32)`, computed in f32, cast back on `copy_out` ✓ — matches golden's promote→compute→demote path\n- f32 path: `.to(asc.float32)` is identity, matches golden's direct f32 compute ✓\n- inf/nan (cases 12-13): IEEE propagation, no host special-casing ✓\n- scalar=0.0 (case 17): `div * 0.0` — x2/x3 is finite (x3≥0.1), so finite*0=0, x1+0=x1 ✓\n- scalar placement: `div_tile * scalar` (scalar on right) ✓\n\n**6. UB budget at TILE=1024**\n- f16/bf16 path: ~10 visible tiles (3 input @2B + 6 f32 @4B + 1 cast-back @2B) = ~36864 B; ×2 unroll = ~74 KB; ×1.6 overhead ≈ 115 KB < 253952 B ✓\n- f32 path: ~10 tiles @4B = 40960 B; ×2 = ~82 KB; ×1.6 ≈ 131 KB < 253952 B ✓\n\n**7. All 20 case routes — dispatch & compile**\n- Cases 1-20: list lengths 1-4, ranks 1D-5D, all flatten to 1-D `size = numel()`. `asc.ceildiv(size, 1024)` gives valid `num_tiles`; tail handles non-aligned sizes (e.g. case 12: size=1000003, 976*1024=999424, tail n=579) ✓\n- 3 unique specializations (f32/f16/bf16), all fit UB ✓\n- `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` — all cases have num_tiles ≥ 1, so cores ≥ 1 ✓\n\n**8. Anti-cheat**\n- No torch math ops; only `empty_like`, `is_contiguous`, `contiguous`, `numel` ✓\n- No `.to(dtype)` on device tensors (cast is in-kernel on tiles) ✓\n- No `data_ptr` caching ✓\n\n**9. No forbidden JIT constructs**\n- No `print`, `import`, `break`/`continue`, `return`, `try/except`, `lambda`, `global`, `math.*`, nested functions, or Python `range()` inside `@asc2.jit` ✓\n- Host-side `continue` (for size==0) is in the wrapper, not the kernel ✓\n\nThe candidate is correct against the contract and all 20 routes. No fixes needed. Running the syntax check:","time":{"start":1788348678193,"end":1788348692185}}}
